        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dc6115a5-e15b-5358-8ea1-622dcfe0ef6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hank Aaron, Ozzie Smith, Satchel Paige, Omar Vizquel\n- Places: Mobile, Alabama\n- Roles: shortstop\n- Awards: NL Gold Glove Award\n- Topics: baseball records, defensive achievements\n\nFacts:\n- Mobile, Alabama in popular culture includes Hank Aaron, Ozzie Smith, and Satchel Paige in its list.\n- Ozzie Smith was nicknamed \"The Wizard\" for his defensive brilliance as a shortstop.\n- From 1980 to 1992, Ozzie Smith won the NL Gold Glove Award at shortstop for 13 consecutive seasons.\n- Ozzie Smith set major league records for career assists by a shortstop with 8,375 and for double plays by a shortstop with 1,590.\n- Omar Vizquel later broke Ozzie Smith's major league record for double plays by a shortstop.\n- Ozzie Smith also set the National League record for career games at shortstop with 2,511.",
